1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:13,310
This video shows you how to ask the agent for a pipeline, and how to follow what it does. Here we ask it to parse FortiGate traffic logs, map them to Elastic Common Schema, and route them to Elasticsearch.

2
00:00:13,360 --> 00:00:20,308
This FortiGate source is receiving traffic logs, but the Status page says no route took its stream.

3
00:00:22,920 --> 00:00:24,763
Open the agent.

4
00:00:31,640 --> 00:00:34,721
Tell it what you want, in plain words.

5
00:00:48,360 --> 00:00:50,174
Send.

6
00:00:50,360 --> 00:00:56,710
It starts by reading the configuration: which group runs the source, and what already exists.

7
00:00:56,760 --> 00:01:04,185
It finds no samples, so it captures twenty real records from the source, and saves them on a new branch.

8
00:01:10,760 --> 00:01:18,137
Then it reads the documentation it needs: the parser, the syslog receiver, and the language reference.

9
00:01:35,760 --> 00:01:40,910
Each indented line is one request it made, with the status that came back.

10
00:01:40,960 --> 00:01:51,150
With what it learned, it writes a plan. The plan is to strip the syslog priority, read the key value pairs, and map them to Elastic Common Schema.

11
00:01:51,200 --> 00:01:54,630
It saves the pipeline and the route on its branch.

12
00:01:54,680 --> 00:01:59,743
Then it checks its own work, with a route preview over the sample.

13
00:02:11,200 --> 00:02:14,990
All twenty records match the route, with no exceptions.

14
00:02:15,040 --> 00:02:18,910
Nothing is deployed. The branch waits for you to review it.

15
00:02:18,960 --> 00:02:26,910
Under Things to know, it tells you what it chose. Here, the original FortiGate fields stay beside the new ones.

16
00:02:26,960 --> 00:02:28,850
Check on learning.

17
00:02:29,050 --> 00:02:32,420
Where does the agent put what it builds?

18
00:02:36,820 --> 00:02:42,125
On a branch. Nothing runs until you approve and deploy it.

19
00:02:43,025 --> 00:02:46,599
Where did the records it tested with come from?

20
00:02:50,999 --> 00:02:54,149
A capture it ran on the live source.

21
00:02:55,049 --> 00:02:59,202
Next, you review what the agent built, and deploy it.
